<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP oil and gas output falls in Jan.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP oil and gas output falls in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP) said on Tuesday its oil and condensate production for January slipped to 5.2 million barrels, five percent lower than year earlier.</p>
<p>However, year-to-date oil and condensate production rose compared to a year ago, due mainly to higher European output and relatively stable production from Australian and Asian fields, BHP said.</p>
<p>Gas production eased compared with January 1996 and, on a year-to-date basis, primarily as a result of the sale of producing properties in the Americas, BHP said.</p>
</text>
